---
import Enrollment from "../components/Enrollment.astro";
import ScheduleTour from "../components/ScheduleTour.astro";
import Tuition from "../components/Tuition.astro";
import AboutLayout from "../layouts/AboutLayout.astro";
---

<AboutLayout title="Enrollment Information | Wild Pear Preschool & Summer Camp">
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16">
    <h1>Enrollment Information</h1>
    <div class="text-muted-foreground mt-4 space-y-4 text-pretty">
      <p>
        Enrolling at Wild Pear starts with getting to know each other, not paperwork. Below
        you'll find everything you need in one place: our hours and school year calendar,
        current tuition rates, and a full walkthrough of the enrollment process from your first
        tour to your child's first day. We don't enroll on a first-come-first-served basis, so
        there's no need to rush; we take time to build small, well-balanced classroom cohorts and
        are happy to answer questions along the way. If anything below is unclear, <a
          href="/contact"
          class="text-primary-accent underline underline-offset-4 hover:no-underline"
          >just reach out</a
        > and we'll walk you through it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Enrollment />

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl space-y-12 px-4 pb-16">
    <div>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">
        School Year Hours and Dates of Operation
      </h2>
      <div class="text-muted-foreground mt-4 space-y-4 text-pretty">
        <p>
          Wild Pear offers childcare for up to 16 children, ages 1-5 years old,
          during the school year. We are open Monday through Friday from 7:30am
          to 5:30pm.
        </p>
        <p>
          Our school year typically begins in early September on the Thursday
          after Labor Day and runs until mid-June. During this time we are
          closed for two weeks of winter break, one week of spring break, along
          with two family conference days, two inservice days, and all major
          holidays. A calendar of specific closure dates is given to families
          when they enroll and can be found in our family handbook.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <Tuition />

    <div>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Enrollment Process</h2>

      <div class="mt-6">
        <h3 class="text-foreground text-lg font-semibold">Tour</h3>
        <div class="text-muted-foreground mt-2 space-y-4 text-pretty">
          <p>
            Wild Pear does not enroll families without a tour. We want to show
            you around and be able to chat and answer any questions you may
            have. It's also very important for us to meet the child (or
            children) you are hoping to enroll in our program (with an
            exception, of course, for children yet to be born).
          </p>
          <p>
            All families who have applied will be invited to come out and join
            one of multiple group tours offered in early spring (generally in
            the first few weekends of April). Typically, this is where we meet
            all the families that we end up enrolling for the upcoming school
            year. Should a slot become available mid-school-year, we will
            consider which family would be the best fit and reach out to them
            directly to schedule a tour. Because tours take significant time and
            energy, we are often unable to coordinate individual tours for
            families who are unable to make it to the group tours in spring.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-6">
        <h3 class="text-foreground text-lg font-semibold">Application</h3>
        <div class="text-muted-foreground mt-2 space-y-4 text-pretty">
          <p>
            Families wishing to enroll their child at Wild Pear can submit a
            simple application, which includes a completed Application for
            Enrollment and a non-refundable $20 fee. Applying for enrollment
            does not guarantee enrollment at a later date. It does, however,
            guarantee that the child will be invited for a tour and be
            considered for enrollment in open slots as they become available.
          </p>
          <p>
            We do not enroll on a first-come-first-served basis. Instead, we
            have a goal to create well-balanced and diverse cohorts of children
            while striving to coordinate each family's preferred schedule. For
            this reason, we do ask that parents give us as much information as
            possible on their application form and notify us of any changes that
            come up. Since we can't possibly weigh and balance all the potential
            cohort variations until after we hold tours, we are unable to tell
            families the "odds" of them being accepted. Some families get
            invited to enroll right after applying, and for others it may take a
            few years.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>


      <div class="mt-6">
        <h3 class="text-foreground text-lg font-semibold">Enrollment</h3>
        <div class="text-muted-foreground mt-2 space-y-4 text-pretty">
          <p>
            We enroll children into cohorts based on how old they will be by
            September 1st. They will move through Wild Pear together with this
            cohort and eventually graduate and move to kindergarten at the same
            time. Our infant cohort might have 1-2 children who will all be 1 by
            September and turn 2 during the school year. Our toddler cohort will
            have between 2-4 children who will all be 2 by September and turn 3
            during the school year. Our younger preschool cohort will have 5-6
            children who will all be 3 by September and turn 4 during the school
            year, and the older preschool cohort will have 5-6 children who will
            all be 4 turning 5.
          </p>
          <p>
            Typically, families are notified of their enrollment status by
            mid-May. Once offered a slot, families will need to choose to either
            enroll or pass. If they choose to pass, the slot will be offered to
            another family. In most cases, families will have up to one week to
            decide if they want the available slot. If they decide to enroll,
            they will need to pay a $500 non-refundable deposit, which will hold
            their slot until September 1st. $300 of the deposit will cover the
            annual enrollment fee, while $200 will be applied to September's
            tuition.
          </p>
          <p>
            Enrolling in our summer camp works a little differently, since it's a seasonal
            program with its own cancellation timeline. See the <a
              href="/programs/summer-camp#cancellation-policy"
              class="text-primary-accent underline underline-offset-4 hover:no-underline"
              >summer camp cancellation policy</a
            > for details on refund eligibility.
          </p>
          <p>
            Anyone who does not get an offer to enroll will continue to be
            considered for any unexpected mid-year openings that arise, and will
            be invited to attend a group tour again the following spring.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Fees and Deposits</h2>
      <div class="text-muted-foreground mt-4 space-y-4 text-pretty">
        <p>
          We encourage everyone to pay online through Zelle by tagging our email
          address. (It may show up as Wild Primrose Preschool, that's still us!)
          We also accept personal checks and cashier's checks, which can be
          placed in the mail box.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">
        Changing Schedules & Adding Siblings
      </h2>
      <div class="text-muted-foreground mt-4 space-y-4 text-pretty">
        <p>
          We know that sometimes families may be willing to accept a slot that
          isn't totally ideal, or may need to change their enrollment schedule
          mid-school-year. Anytime a family wants to decrease the number of days
          they are enrolled, they will need to give 30 days' written notice and
          can shift to their new schedule after the 30 days is up. If a family
          wants to swap days or increase their enrollment, they need to send us
          an email right away, and their schedule request will be put on top of
          a list for consideration should anything shift mid-school-year.
        </p>
        <p>
          When enrolling new students, priority is given to families with
          siblings who are currently enrolled at Wild Pear and/or alumni
          families. If you'd like to enroll a sibling, please fill out an
          Application Form and turn it in right away — no fee is required! If
          the sibling you'd like to enroll will be under 12 months in September,
          please know we may be able to make an exception for your family, so
          please ask.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <ScheduleTour />
</AboutLayout>
